You will be shown a series of C code snippets, which you should try to comprehend. 
For each snippet please type the standard output of the program, emitted by the printf function. 
If you are unsure about an answer or part of an answer you can instead respond with ?.
If you believe that a snippet produces no output or that its full output cannot be sensibly determined respond with _.

You see the snippet:

void main() {
   int V1 = 288;

   char V2 = V1 % 256;

   printf("%d\n", V2);
}

Your answer: << c >>.
